## COMP605 Assignment 4

## Assignment 4 – Instructions
Discussions on Real-Life Project Management Experiences
Weight: 15% of your final grade
This assignment comprises two main tasks:
1.	Write a posting in the Assignment 4 Discussion that discusses a real-life project management experience (50 marks).
2.	Discuss your peers’ real-life project management experiences and answer questions/comments from your peers on your real-life project management experience in the Assignment 4 Discussion (50 marks).

## Writing About a Real-Life Project Management Experience
The purpose of this assignment is to share and discuss real-life project management experiences. As a first step in sharing a real-life project management experience, you need to find an example of an information technology project that went well or one that did not go so well. This could be either a project that you have been involved in and where you share your own experience with your peers, or it could be a project that you know of or have read about.
In your posting, you must:
1.	provide a brief description of the scope of the project;
2.	explain the organizational background and how the project was implemented;
3.	provide information on whether the project was successful or not; and
4.	provide some reasons why the project went well or did not go well.
Make sure that you post your real-life project management experience at the latest by the end of Week 9.

## Discussion of Real-Life Project Management Experiences
Towards the end of Week 9 and during Weeks 10 and 11, discussions on the postings of all students will take place. These discussions include comments and questions to your peers’ real-life project management experiences as well as answers and comments to your peers’ questions and comments on your real-life project management experience.
You are required to write at least four postings in this part of the assignment. These postings can be:
•	comments or questions to your peers’ real-life project management experiences; and
•	answers and comments to your peers’ questions and comments on your real-life project management experience.
Make sure that your comments, questions and answers are posted at the latest by the end of Week 11!

## Grading Criteria
The posting of your real-life project management experience will be graded based on the completeness and clarity of the example, and is worth 50% of the assignment grade.
The discussions about your peers’ real-life project management experiences and answers to your peers’ questions and comments on your real-life project management experience will be graded based on the number and meaningfulness of your postings, and is worth 50% of the assignment grade.
